        "id": "l_BwDqnWcdjT"
      },
      "source": [
        "# How to Access GES DISC Kerchunk Files\n",
        "\n",
        "### Updated: 5/29/2026\n",
        "\n",
        "### Overview\n",
        "\n",
        "This Jupyter Notebook demonstrates how to access GPM_L3 and MERRA-2 “Kerchunk” files, a format for dataset virtualization. It shows the use of the Earthdata Login widget to authenticate with Earthdata Login servers, access a single [M2T1NXSLV.5.12.4](https://cmr.earthdata.nasa.gov/search/concepts/C1276812863-GES_DISC.html) Kerchunk file to demonstrate 2-meter temperature over Los Angeles during January 2010, and access and concatenate two [GPM_3IMERGDF.07](https://data.nasa.gov/dataset/gpm-imerg-final-precipitation-l3-1-day-0-1-degree-x-0-1-degree-v07-gpm-3imergdf-at-ges-dis-13ed8) Kerchunk files to plot MWPrecipitation values over Chicago during the 2011 Groundhog Day Blizzard and the corresponding \"baseline\" period in the previous year.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Prerequisites\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"background:#FFFFC5; border:1px solid #000000; padding:5px 10px; color:#000000;\">\n",
        "    <strong>Note:</strong> The performance of this notebook depends on the number of CPU cores, available memory, and internet bandwidth of the compute instance.<br />\n",
        "    If a query exceeds these resources, performance may be significantly degraded. In such cases, an alternative subsetting approach such as\n",
        "    <a href=\"https://github.com/nasa/gesdisc-tutorials/blob/main/notebooks/How_to_Search_and_Load_Cloud_OPeNDAP.ipynb\" target=\"_blank\">Cloud OPeNDAP</a>\n",
        "    or the\n",
        "    <a href=\"https://github.com/nasa/gesdisc-tutorials/blob/main/notebooks/How_to_Subset_and_Download_L234_Data_Using_Python.ipynb\" target=\"_blank\">GES DISC Subsetter API</a>\n",
        "    should be considered.\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook requires Python >=3.12 and the following libraries:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Valid Earthdata Login credentials\n",
        "- [xarray](https://docs.xarray.dev/en/stable/) (must be >=2025.4.0)\n",
        "- [earthaccess](https://earthaccess.readthedocs.io/en/latest/quick-start/) (must be >=0.16)\n",
        "- [terra_ui_components](https://github.com/nasa/terra-ui-components)\n",
        "- [Pandas](https://pandas.pydata.org/) (must be <3.x)\n",
        "- [Pyarrow](https://arrow.apache.org/docs/python/index.html) (must be exactly 23.0.1)\n",
        "- [fsspec](https://filesystem-spec.readthedocs.io/en/latest/)\n",
        "- [Zarr](https://zarr.readthedocs.io/en/stable/)\n",
        "- [Dask.distributed](https://distributed.dask.org/en/stable/)\n",
        "- [Matplotlib](https://matplotlib.org/)\n",
        "- [Kerchunk](https://fsspec.github.io/kerchunk/)\n",
        "- [Fastparquet](https://fastparquet.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) (must be exactly 2026.3.0)\n",
        "- [s3fs](https://s3fs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/)\n",
        "- [h5py](https://docs.h5py.org/en/stable/)\n",
        "- [Virtualizarr](https://virtualizarr.readthedocs.io/en/stable/)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Recommended Anaconda Environment YAML:\n",
        "We ***strongly*** recommend installing the ['nasa-gesdisc-kerchunk' YAML file](https://github.com/nasa/gesdisc-tutorials/tree/main/environments/nasa-gesdisc-kerchunk.yml) provided in the 'environments' subfolder to run this notebook. \n",
        "Please follow the instructions [here](https://conda.io/projects/conda/en/latest/user-guide/tasks/manage-environments.html#creating-an-environment-from-an-environment-yml-file) to install and activate this environment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "971zqlAIcgwk"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 1. Import Libraries"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 11,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "etE8XFjDKYwS"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import warnings\n",
        "import earthaccess\n",
        "import xarray as xr\n",
        "import dask\n",
        "from dask.distributed import Client\n",
        "from terra_ui_components import TerraEarthdataLogin\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "%matplotlib inline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-KaiXUxVcjJL"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 2. Create Dask Workers\n",
        "\n",
        "Change the number of workers (`n_workers`) based on your CPU core count."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "bCNLdvK_KqKb",
        "outputId": "2048968c-50fc-4c22-bb74-0d47599d13b5"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "client = Client(\n",
        "    n_workers=8,\n",
        "    threads_per_worker=1,\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "r9vVVQWwcqmt"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 3. Authenticate and Create Virtual Dataset Loader Function"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 216,
          "referenced_widgets": [
            "30b1a4e88c2e41aca950d8920093ccb0",
            "ce04845540484d8ea00d294ec134a7bd"
          ]
        },
        "id": "IYS1qWc_K7m7",
        "outputId": "ab46f611-8c26-40c4-df83-6ace7143ea4b"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Authenticate using Earthdata Login Widget\n",
        "auth = TerraEarthdataLogin()\n",
        "display(auth)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create virtual dataset loader function\n",
        "def get_vds(parq: str, chunks: dict={}, **kwargs):\n",
        "    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n",
        "        warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\", category=xr.SerializationWarning)\n",
        "        return xr.open_dataset(\n",
        "            \"reference://\",\n",
        "            engine=\"zarr\",\n",
        "            chunks=chunks,\n",
        "            backend_kwargs={\n",
        "                \"storage_options\": {\n",
        "                    \"fo\": str(parq),\n",
        "                    \"remote_protocol\": \"https\",\n",
        "                    \"asynchronous\": True,\n",
        "                    \"remote_options\": {\n",
        "                        \"headers\": {\"Authorization\": f'Bearer {auth.bearerToken}'},\n",
        "                        \"asynchronous\": True,\n",
        "                    }\n",
        "                },\n",
        "                \"consolidated\": True\n",
        "            },\n",
        "            **kwargs\n",
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "D3stT49Icwov"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 4. Load a Single MERRA-2 Kerchunk File\n",
        "\n",
        "Here, we will load a single Kerchunk file of M2T1NXSLV.5.12.4 for 2010. Note that this will only take a few seconds to run, since we have only loaded the metadata of the virtualized chunks. No actual data is loaded until we run Xarray compute functions in later cells.\n",
        "\n",
        "A list of available collections and instructions to format a different Kerchunk URL can be found here: https://github.com/nasa/gesdisc-tutorials/blob/main/user-guidance/TDS_to_VDS.md#available-collections"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 14,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "ljb2vf2NLCJs",
        "outputId": "52a85d0e-65d6-46de-8789-f5cf11df7606"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "<xarray.Dataset> Size: 685GB\n",
            "Dimensions:   (time: 8760, lat: 361, lon: 576)\n",
            "Coordinates:\n",
            "  * time      (time) datetime64[ns] 70kB 2010-01-01T00:30:00 ... 2010-12-31T2...\n",
            "  * lat       (lat) float64 3kB -90.0 -89.5 -89.0 -88.5 ... 88.5 89.0 89.5 90.0\n",
            "  * lon       (lon) float64 5kB -180.0 -179.4 -178.8 ... 178.1 178.8 179.4\n",
            "Data variables: (12/47)\n",
            "    CLDPRS    (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    CLDTMP    (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    DISPH     (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    H1000     (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    H250      (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    H500      (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    ...        ...\n",
            "    V250      (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    V2M       (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    V500      (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    V50M      (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    V850      (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    ZLCL      (time, lat, lon) float64 15GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 91, 144), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "Attributes: (12/25)\n",
            "    Conventions:                       CF-1\n",
            "    Institution:                       NASA Global Modeling and Assimilation ...\n",
            "    References:                        http://gmao.gsfc.nasa.gov\n",
            "    Format:                            NetCDF-4/HDF-5\n",
            "    SpatialCoverage:                   global\n",
            "    VersionID:                         5.12.4\n",
            "    ...                                ...\n",
            "    Contact:                           http://gmao.gsfc.nasa.gov\n",
            "    identifier_product_doi:            10.5067/VJAFPLI1CSIV\n",
            "    RangeBeginningDate:                2010-01-01\n",
            "    RangeBeginningTime:                00:00:00.000000\n",
            "    RangeEndingDate:                   2010-12-31\n",
            "    RangeEndingTime:                   23:59:59.000000\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "vds = get_vds(\"https://data.gesdisc.earthdata.nasa.gov/browse/kerchunk/MERRA2/M2T1NXSLV.5.12.4/2010.parq\")\n",
        "print(vds)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0mnWvPhec45P"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 5. Create Time Series of Surface Temperature Over Los Angeles for January 2010\n",
        "\n",
        "This cell may take some time to run since we actually manifest the virtualized data to our compute instance when we call `compute()`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 15,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 427
        },
        "id": "rdykzy6-SrkO",
        "outputId": "96420c0c-6da1-42e4-fe40-f4acc848a203"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "[<matplotlib.lines.Line2D at 0x189fbea50>]"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 15,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1200x400 with 1 Axes>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "ts = vds['T2M'] \\\n",
        "    .sel(time=slice(\"2010-01-01\",\"2010-01-31\")) \\\n",
        "    .sel(lat=34.05, lon=-118.24, method=\"nearest\") \\\n",
        "    .compute()\n",
        "\n",
        "ts.plot(figsize=(12, 4))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6. Concatenate Two GPM_3IMERGDF.07 Kerchunk Files\n",
        "\n",
        "The `xr.concat` function can be used to concatenate two virtual dataset objects into a single virtual dataset. Here, we load GPM_IMERGDF.07 data from 2010-01-01 to 2011-12-31 and concatenate along the `time` dimension.\n",
        "\n",
        "We will need to manually update the `BeginDate` and `EndDate` attributes to show the correct temporal length of the virtual dataset."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 16,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "<xarray.Dataset> Size: 170GB\n",
            "Dimensions:                         (time: 730, lon: 3600, lat: 1800, nv: 2)\n",
            "Coordinates:\n",
            "  * time                            (time) datetime64[ns] 6kB 2010-01-01 ... ...\n",
            "  * lon                             (lon) float32 14kB -179.9 -179.9 ... 179.9\n",
            "  * lat                             (lat) float64 14kB -89.95 -89.85 ... 89.95\n",
            "Dimensions without coordinates: nv\n",
            "Data variables:\n",
            "    MWprecipitation                 (time, lon, lat) float32 19GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 3600, 900), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    MWprecipitation_cnt             (time, lon, lat) float32 19GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 3600, 900), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    MWprecipitation_cnt_cond        (time, lon, lat) float32 19GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 3600, 900), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    precipitation                   (time, lon, lat) float32 19GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 3600, 900), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    precipitation_cnt               (time, lon, lat) float32 19GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 3600, 900), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    precipitation_cnt_cond          (time, lon, lat) float32 19GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 3600, 900), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    probabilityLiquidPrecipitation  (time, lon, lat) float32 19GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 3600, 900), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    randomError                     (time, lon, lat) float32 19GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 3600, 900), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    randomError_cnt                 (time, lon, lat) float32 19GB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 3600, 900), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "    time_bnds                       (time, nv) datetime64[ns] 12kB dask.array<chunksize=(1, 2), meta=np.ndarray>\n",
            "Attributes:\n",
            "    BeginDate:  2010-01-01\n",
            "    BeginTime:  00:00:00.000Z\n",
            "    EndDate:    2011-12-31\n",
            "    EndTime:    23:59:59.999Z\n",
            "    title:      GPM IMERG Final Precipitation L3 1 day 0.1 degree x 0.1 degre...\n",
            "    DOI:        10.5067/GPM/IMERGDF/DAY/07\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "vds_1 = get_vds(\"https://data.gesdisc.earthdata.nasa.gov/browse/kerchunk/GPM_L3/GPM_3IMERGDF.07/2010.parq\")\n",
        "vds_2 = get_vds(\"https://data.gesdisc.earthdata.nasa.gov/browse/kerchunk/GPM_L3/GPM_3IMERGDF.07/2011.parq\")\n",
        "\n",
        "vds_concat = xr.concat([vds_1, vds_2], dim=\"time\")\n",
        "vds_concat.attrs[\"BeginDate\"] = str(vds_concat.time.min().dt.date.values)\n",
        "vds_concat.attrs[\"EndDate\"] = str(vds_concat.time.max().dt.date.values)\n",
        "print(vds_concat)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 7. Query a Single Point over Chicago\n",
        "\n",
        "We will select the nearest point over Chicago, the `MWprecipitation` variable, and the period from 01-28 to 02-05 for both 2010 and 2011."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 17,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "lat = 41.87\n",
        "lon = -87.62\n",
        "\n",
        "point = vds_concat[\"MWprecipitation\"].sel(\n",
        "    lat=lat,\n",
        "    lon=lon,\n",
        "    method=\"nearest\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "blizzard_2011 = point.sel(time=slice(\"2011-01-28\", \"2011-02-05\"))\n",
        "baseline_2010 = point.sel(time=slice(\"2010-01-28\", \"2010-02-05\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 8. Compare Daily Average Precipitation Rates by Day of Year"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 18,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1200x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Convert to pandas index\n",
        "t1 = pd.to_datetime(blizzard_2011.time.values)\n",
        "t2 = pd.to_datetime(baseline_2010.time.values)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Day of year (1–365/366)\n",
        "x1 = t1.dayofyear\n",
        "x2 = t2.dayofyear\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 5))\n",
        "\n",
        "ax.plot(x1, blizzard_2011.values,\n",
        "        label=\"2011 Blizzard\", linewidth=1.5)\n",
        "\n",
        "ax.plot(x2, baseline_2010.values,\n",
        "        label=\"2010 Baseline\", linewidth=1.5)\n",
        "\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Precipitation Rate (mm/hr) Comparison for 01-08 to 02-05, 2010 and 2011\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Day of Year\")\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"mm/hr\")\n",
        "\n",
        "ax.legend()\n",
        "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    }
  ],
